# Mobile layout lock

Do **not** change mobile sizing, viewport setup, or responsive breakpoints unless the user explicitly asks.

## Locked (no edits without approval)

- `viewport` meta tag (`width=device-width`, keep `viewport-fit=cover` where present)
- Full-screen heights: use `100dvh`, not `100vh`, on app shells
- `env(safe-area-inset-*)` on headers, footers, fixed UI, and PWA overlays
- Existing `@media` breakpoints — do not rename, remove, or shift them
- **saifglobal16.info**: geo map mobile layout and visual design stay locked

## When adding UI

- Match the project's existing mobile patterns
- Use `flex-wrap` / stacked layouts; never squeeze desktop nav onto small screens
- Fixed bars must respect safe-area; no horizontal overflow at ~375px width

## This project (saiftechglobal.com)

- Breakpoints: mobile default → `768px` nav/grid → `1024px` products → `1200px` four-column products
- Mobile menu (`#mobile-nav`) stays; desktop `.site-nav` hidden below 768px
- Do not change `hero-actions` wrap behavior or remove mobile-only nav links
